  "body": "CHECK-039 REVISE. Filed-point arithmetic reproduces: 13,176 numeric-field comparisons, 39 headline comparisons and 54 validation checks pass; all 31 input pins match. No owner code read or run. Each concept’s least SF and the original O5 0.689108/+1329.818726 kg points reproduce.\nIndependent continuous reconstruction finds better C2b O5 points under the same assumptions: fixed-mass SF 0.699691806, and +1127.071353 kg at least SF 1.000001080, reducing the filed deficit by 202.747373 kg. Two starts agree; constructive points pass the original threshold rules. These are feasible model points, not a global optimum or a floating hull.\nCR-62257, IDH p4.1.012 and SP-8032 p24 checked at primary pages. The .425 recommendation exists; psi>=28 and gamma_s>=10 are model gates, not handbook thresholds. Composite gamma_s 10.400 differs from isolated tube EI/(aD)=3.197. Cap mapping, omitted wavelengths and SiC thermal joint forces remain projections.\nCorrect plain-Ti 317/917 to .345692; STA8.1’s 759k/754k predictions describe different refinements. Separate fixed-mass seam failures from the mass-added point, where today’s Q/scarf/tube screens already pass. Four compact gs5 shapes require disclosed psi-based recovery. Ten actionable NFI rows, exact arithmetic, source pins and constructive designs filed. No successor or out-of-band contact.",
